cap-fmu (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix intermittent failure to re-engage AUTO after a fresh mission upload
    (goto or search): the aircraft could remain in RTL indefinitely due to a
    race between the mode change and ArduPilot's post-upload mission reset.
  * Track GPS fix validity (GPS_RAW_INT.fix_type) and report it to FSS, so a
    degraded or lost GPS fix is no longer indistinguishable from a fresh,
    current position.
  * Latch flight termination: once triggered, no later command can silently
    move the FMU back out of the terminated state.
  * Fix a paused search's progress being corrupted by a goto mission's own
    MISSION_ITEM_REACHED (including its RTL terminator).
  * Rate-limit ADS-B rebroadcast to one update per ICAO address per second,
    so a busy receiver near a real airport cannot flood the autopilot.
  * Make the low-battery latch's debounce count configurable (previously a
    hardcoded constant), alongside the existing lowbat_threshold.
  * Warn instead of silently losing a goto mission upload interrupted by a
    MAV link drop; log and replay a failed SMM-triggered RTL on link
    recovery.
  * Fail hard on an unopenable or unparsable client.json instead of a
    reassuring "using defaults" warning immediately followed by a fatal
    error.
  * Scrub SMM credential buffers after use instead of leaving them in
    non-zeroed heap memory.
  * Rotate fmu.log once a size threshold is crossed, not only at process
    start, so a long-running or chatty deployment can't grow one log file
    without bound.
  * Route MAV/SMM/aircraft-tracking diagnostics through the persistent,
    rotating logger instead of stdout/stderr, which a daemon typically
    discards.
  * Docker: generate the FSS client config safely via jq instead of shell
    string interpolation, create/chown the log directory so logging works
    for the non-root container user, and support a LOG_DIR override.

 -- Scott Parlane <sjp@canterburyairpatrol.org>  Sun, 05 Jul 2026 19:52:32 +1200

cap-fmu (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First stable release.
  * Configurable FMU behaviour via the optional "fmu" block in client.json
    (altitude cap/floor in metres or feet, camera field of view, low-battery
    threshold, reconnect interval, and log level).
  * Search altitude derived from the search sweep width and camera field of
    view, clamped to the configured [floor, cap] range.
  * Required --terminate-action argument (none, disarm, or terminate) selects
    the airframe-appropriate flight-termination behaviour.
  * Debounced low-battery RTL latch: the latch only engages after several
    consecutive low readings, so a single spurious sample cannot ground the
    mission.
  * Failsafe RTL on loss of FSS or autopilot (MAVLink heartbeat) comms.

 -- Scott Parlane <sjp@canterburyairpatrol.org>  Sun, 14 Jun 2026 12:12:52 +1200
